# Lifting State Up ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

    ## 🤯 Problem

    Imagine you have two components.

    Cart

    ↓

    Cart Item

    ↓

    Total Price

    When the quantity changes in Cart Item,

    the Total Price should also update.

    But...

    Both components need the same data.

    React says:

    Move the state to their common Parent.

    This is called Lifting State Up.

    ---

    ## 🧠 Think Like This

    One data.

    ↓

    Many components need it.

    ↓

    Keep it in the Parent.

    ---

    ## ✅ What is it?

    Lifting State Up means moving the state from a Child component to its nearest common Parent.

    The Parent becomes the owner of the data and shares it with other components using Props.

    ---

    ## 🤔 Why do we use it?

    Whenever multiple components need the same data.

    Examples:

    - Shopping Cart
    - Student List
    - Dashboard Filters
    - Employee List
    - Search Feature

    ---

    ## 🧠 Never Forget This

    👨‍👩‍👧 Family

    Imagine two children need money.

    Instead of one child giving money to another,

    the Father keeps the money.

    Whenever a child needs it,

    the Father gives it.

    Parent = Father

    Children = Components

    State stays with the Parent.

    ---

    ## 💼 Real Project

    School ERP

    Student Search Box

    ↓

    Student List

    ↓

    Student Details

    User searches

    ↓

    Student List updates

    ↓

    Student Details also updates.

    Instead of both components having separate state,

    the Parent stores the search value

    and passes it to both components.

    ---

    ## ⚠ Interview Trap

    ❌ Don't copy the same state into multiple components.

    One source of truth is enough.

    Keep the state in the Parent.

    ---

    ## 💻 Pattern

    ```jsx
    const [search, setSearch] = useState("");

    <SearchBox search={search} setSearch={setSearch} />
    <StudentList search={search} />
    ```

    ---

    ## 🔄 Angular Brain

    Think of it like keeping shared data in a Parent Component

    and passing it using @Input().

    ---

    ## 🎤 Interview Answer

    Lifting State Up means moving shared state to the nearest common Parent component so multiple Child components can use the same data through Props.

    ---

    ## 📝 Keywords

    Parent

    Shared State

    Props

    Common Parent

    Single Source of Truth 
