# Prop Drilling ⭐⭐⭐⭐☆

## 🤯 Problem

Imagine your component structure.

App

↓

Dashboard

↓

Sidebar

↓

Profile

↓

User Name

The User Name is needed only in the Profile.

But...

React forces you to pass it through

Dashboard

↓

Sidebar

↓

Profile

Even though Dashboard and Sidebar don't use it.

This problem is called Prop Drilling.

---

## 🧠 Think Like This

Imagine your Mom wants to give ₹100 to your younger brother.

Instead of giving it directly,

she gives it to you.

↓

You give it to your sister.

↓

Your sister gives it to your brother.

Everyone is just passing the money.

Nobody is using it.

This is Prop Drilling.

---

## ✅ What is it?

Prop Drilling means passing the same data through multiple components just to reach the component that actually needs it.

Intermediate components simply forward the data.

They don't use it.

---

## 🤔 Why is it a Problem?

Because:

- Too much passing
- More code
- Hard to maintain
- Difficult to understand

As the application grows,

Prop Drilling becomes messy.

---

## 🧠 Never Forget This

📦 Parcel Delivery

App has a parcel.

↓

Dashboard receives it.

↓

Sidebar receives it.

↓

Profile receives it.

Only Profile opens the parcel.

Everyone else just passes it.

That's Prop Drilling.

---

## 💼 Real Project

School ERP

Logged-in Teacher

↓

App

↓

Dashboard

↓

Sidebar

↓

Header

↓

Profile

Only Profile needs the Teacher Name.

But every component has to receive and pass it.

This is Prop Drilling.

---

## ⚠ Interview Trap

❌ Don't use Context API for every small piece of data.

If only one or two components need the data,

Props are perfectly fine.

Use Context when many components need the same data across different levels.

---

## 💻 Pattern

```jsx
<App user={user} />

<Dashboard user={user} />

<Sidebar user={user} />

<Profile user={user} />
```

Every component passes user,

but only Profile actually uses it.

---

## 🔄 Angular Brain

Think of passing the same @Input()

through multiple components

until it reaches the final child.

Instead,

Angular developers often use a Shared Service.

React solves this using Context API.

---

## 🎤 Interview Answer

Prop Drilling is the process of passing data through multiple intermediate components to reach a deeply nested component. It makes the code difficult to maintain. React Context API helps solve this problem.

---

## 📝 Keywords

Props

Intermediate Components

Nested Components

Context API

Shared Data
