# Context API ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

## 🤯 Problem

Imagine your app has:

App

↓

Dashboard

↓

Sidebar

↓

Profile

↓

User Name

The User Name is needed in Profile.

Without Context API,

you have to pass it through every component.

↓

App

↓

Dashboard

↓

Sidebar

↓

Profile

This is Prop Drilling.

React says:

Keep the data in one common place.

Any component can access it.

This is Context API.

---

## 🧠 Think Like This

One cupboard.

↓

Everyone in the house can take things from it.

No need to pass the item room by room.

---

## ✅ What is it?

Context API is React's way of sharing data between multiple components.

Instead of passing Props through every component,

React stores the data in a common place.

Any component can access it.

---

## 🤔 Why do we use it?

Whenever many components need the same data.

Examples

- Logged-in User
- Theme (Dark/Light)
- Language
- Company Details
- Permissions

---

## 🧠 Never Forget This

🏫 School Notice Board

Principal writes one notice.

↓

Holiday Tomorrow

↓

Every student reads it.

No teacher has to go class by class.

Context API works exactly the same way.

One place.

Everyone reads.

---

## 💼 Real Project

School ERP

Logged-in Teacher

↓

Navbar

↓

Sidebar

↓

Profile

↓

Attendance

All these components need

Teacher Name

Instead of passing it through every component,

Context API stores it once.

Every component reads it directly.

---

## ⚠ Interview Trap

❌ Don't store everything inside Context API.

Good for:

✅ Logged-in User

✅ Theme

✅ Language

Bad for:

❌ Counter

❌ Input Field

❌ Local Component State

Use useState for local data.

Use Context API for shared data.

---

## 💻 Pattern

```jsx
<UserContext.Provider value={user}>
  <App />
</UserContext.Provider>
```

Read it using

```jsx
const user = useContext(UserContext);
```

---

## 🔄 Angular Brain

Think of it like a Shared Service.

One service stores the data.

Any component can access it.

Context API works the same way.

---

## 🎤 Interview Answer

Context API is used to share common data between multiple components without passing props through every level of the component tree.

---

## 📝 Keywords

Provider

Shared Data

Global Data

useContext

Prop Drilling
