### 📝 Keywords

Store

Global State

configureStore

Central Storage

Redux

## Slice ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

### 🤯 Problem

Imagine your School ERP Store contains:

Store

├── User

├── Students

├── Teachers

├── Fees

├── Attendance

├── Reports

Keeping everything in one file becomes huge and difficult to manage.

React says:

Split the Store into small sections.

Each section is called a Slice.

---

### 🧠 Think Like This

Imagine a School Office.

Instead of one person handling everything,

you have different departments.

Admissions Department

↓

Student Department

↓

Accounts Department

↓

HR Department

Each department handles only its own work.

Redux works the same way.

Each Slice manages only its own data.

---

### ✅ What is it?

A Slice is a small section of the Redux Store.

Each Slice manages one type of data and the logic to update that data.

---

### 🤔 Why do we use it?

To organize the Store into smaller, manageable parts.

Examples

- User Slice
- Student Slice
- Teacher Slice
- Fee Slice
- Attendance Slice
- Notification Slice

---

### 🧠 Never Forget This

🏢 Office Departments

HR

↓

Employees

-----------------------

Accounts

↓

Salary

-----------------------

Admissions

↓

Students

Every department has its own responsibility.

Redux Slice works exactly the same way.

---

### 💼 Real Project

School ERP

Store

↓

User Slice

Stores

- Teacher Name
- Token
- Role

-----------------------

Student Slice

Stores

- Student List
- Selected Student

-----------------------

Fee Slice

Stores

- Fee Details
- Pending Fees

Each Slice manages only its own data.

---

### ⚠ Interview Trap

❌ One Slice should NOT manage everything.

Wrong

Student Slice

↓

Students

Teachers

Fees

Reports

Correct

Student Slice → Students

Teacher Slice → Teachers

Fee Slice → Fees

One Slice = One Responsibility.

---

### 💻 Pattern

```jsx
const userSlice = createSlice({
  name: "user",
  initialState: {
    user: null,
  },
  reducers: {}
});
```

---

### 🔄 Angular Brain

Think of it like NgRx Feature State.

Instead of one huge Store,

Angular divides the Store into Feature States.

Redux calls them Slices.

---

### 🎤 Interview Answer

A Slice is a logical section of the Redux Store. It contains related state and the reducers used to update that state.

